<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3954" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aspectābĭlis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adsp-</span></b> ), e, adj.
		aspecto (perh. only in the foll. exs.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>That may be seen</i>, <i>visible</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Tim. 4</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animal,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Worthy of being seen</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nihil esse aspectabilius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 282, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
